UPSTREAM SOURCES AND THEIR OWN TERMS
------------------------------------
This dataset is derived from public sources, each of which carries its own terms.
Attributing PANTS does not discharge any obligation to those sources.

  UniProt                    Reference sequences, annotations and catalytic-site positions,
                             CC BY 4.0.
  Protein Data Bank (RCSB)   Every experimental structure and its metadata. PDB data are
                             released to the public domain (CC0 1.0). Please cite the PDB
                             alongside this work.
  AlphaFold DB (EMBL-EBI)    Predicted structures fetched by accession, CC BY 4.0. Please
                             cite Jumper et al. 2021 and Varadi et al. 2024.
  PAZy                       The plastics-active enzyme database. An enzyme is listed there
                             because activity on a plastic was measured and published;
                             cite the primary paper, which this release carries as a DOI on
                             every measurement, and PAZy itself.
  ESTHER                     Alpha/beta-hydrolase family assignments, used to select the
                             hard negatives.
  MGnify (EMBL-EBI)          Metagenomic assemblies: the sequence space searched.
  HGMP-SciDB                 Human gut metagenome polyesterases, from the deposit
                             accompanying the paper; see its own terms.

STRUCTURES
----------
Structures under `app/static/` are of three kinds and the distinction is recorded per file
in the database, never inferred from the filename. Experimental structures are redistributed
from the PDB under CC0 and remain citable to their depositors. AlphaFold models are
redistributed under CC BY 4.0. ESMFold predictions were computed here and are covered by
this licence.

A prediction is a hypothesis, not a measurement. The oxyanion hole in a predicted structure
differs systematically from the same protein's crystal structure (paired, n=51, p 1.1e-06),
so predicted and experimental coordinates should not be pooled in a geometric analysis
without accounting for it. The `source` column exists to make that possible.
